# What the host sends, on Cloudflare and on Netlify, which both read this file.
#
# The page carries its own content security policy inside it, and that works on any
# host. The one rule that cannot come from inside a page is the one that refuses to be
# framed, because a browser ignores it when it arrives that way. So it comes from here.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

# Everything the build named with a hash in it. The name changes when the file does,
# so the old one is never asked for again and a year is a safe thing to promise.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
